WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.230
Analysis turns collected information into intelligence by answering the requirement and

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.000
explaining significance.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Organize observations before interpreting them.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Timelines can expose sequence and gaps.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.250
Link analysis can clarify relationships, but a visual connection is not proof of control,

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.000
intent, or wrongdoing.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.985
Test multiple explanations.

00:00:16.985 --> 00:00:20.000
Ask what evidence would be expected if each explanation were true,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.000
and search for both supporting and disconfirming observations.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Be alert to confirmation bias, anchoring on the first result,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
and mistaking absence of public evidence for evidence of absence.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Assign confidence using a consistent method.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.070
Confidence communicates how strongly a judgment is supported by reliable evidence and

00:00:36.070 --> 00:00:37.000
sound reasoning.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.000
It is distinct from impact or urgency.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.160
A high-impact possibility may have low confidence and still justify a measured request for

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:43.951
more information.

00:00:43.951 --> 00:00:47.905
Reports should separate confirmed facts, source claims, analytical judgments,

00:00:47.905 --> 00:00:48.969
and unresolved questions.

00:00:48.969 --> 00:00:51.035
Cite evidence close to the claim it supports.

00:00:51.035 --> 00:00:56.190
Explain limitations such as stale records, uncertain identity, translation issues,

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:58.874
missing primary sources, or possible source coordination.

00:00:58.874 --> 00:01:00.245
Write for the audience.

00:01:00.245 --> 00:01:03.250
Executives may need concise implications and decisions.

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:06.240
Investigators may need a detailed source trail and timeline.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:10.000
Technical teams may need affected assets, indicators, and validation steps.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Avoid unnecessary personal details and dramatic language.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:17.035
A finding is actionable when the recipient understands what happened, why it matters,

00:01:17.035 --> 00:01:20.230
how confident the assessment is, and what proportionate next step is recommended.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:23.860
Responsible reporting also states what could change the judgment and how sensitive

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.380
information should be handled.
